# Kanborg

This document show how to use Kanborg which is a kanban board using git underlying to manage cards/tickets

## 1. Context

- **Working directory**: `~/echo-home.kanborg/codev/kanborg`

## 2. Instructions
- Complete part or full of DAG (makefile) to meet user intent
- Only run a target using **Command** if no dependency found
- If a target has dependencies, make sure all of its dependency targets completed
- If target got failure, do not execute its parent target


## 3. Card Management

### Naming convention

Each card is a markdown file whose name in format: `<PROJECT_CODE>-<ID_NUMBER>.md`

### States

Each card can be in the follow states:

- `BACKLOG`: created
- `TODO`: planned
- `HOLD`: on hold, pending
- `WIP`: work in progress
- `DONE`: completed


## 4. Workflows

### Set working directory

```makefile
set_workdir:
    # Description: Set working directory to make command and data available
    # Command:`cd ~/echo-home.kanborg/codev/kanborg` 
```

### Create new card or project code

```makefile
new_card: set_workdir
    # Description: commit in kanborg
    # Command: `.function/xcard <PROJECT_CODE> <OPTIONAL_DESCRIPTION>`
    # Success: Output path of new card
    # Failure: any error
```

### show kanban board

```makefile
show_kanborg: set_workdir
    # Description: display full kanban board of all cards
    # Command: `.function/show`
    # Success: output in markdown table
    # Failure: any error
```


### Find card

```makefile
find_card: set_workdir
    # Description: Find current state of card or search for path of card
    # Command: `find datum/$(date +%Y) | grep <CARD_NAME>`
    # Success: Output datum/<YEAR>/<CURRENT_STATE>/<CARD_NAME>
    # Failure: No path to card is found
    # Output: path of card
```

### Moving a card
```makefile
move_card: find_card
    # Description: move card from CURRENT_STATE to NEW_STATE
    # Command: `git mv <path of card> datum/$(date +%Y)/{NEW_STATE}`
    # Success: file exists at new path `datum/$(date +%Y)/{NEW_STATE}`
    # Failure: No new path to card is found or error in git command
```

### View a card

```makefile
view_card: find_card
    # Description: view content of card
    # Command: `cat <path_of_card>`
    # Success: output content of card
    # Failure: No content found
    # Input: path of card
    # Output: sections such as <CARD_TITLE>, <DESCRIPTION>, <SOLUTION>, <NOTES>, <TEST>, <JOURNAL> 
```

### Update a card
```makefile
update_card: view_card
    # Description: edit content of card using sed, awk, etc
    # Command: `<edit comand>`
    # Success: new content meet user intent
    # Failure: any error
    # Input: Content of card
```

### Commit Card Changes

```makefile
commit: set_workdir
    # Description: commit in kanborg
    # Command: `.function/commit`
    # Success: new git commit created
    # Failure: error in git command
```

### Run a shell command

```makefile
run_shell_command: set_workdir
    # Description: run external shell command like git, gpul1 to update/manipulate kanborg data
    # Command: `<USER_COMMAND>`
```
